];
---
<!doctype html><html lang="en"><head><meta charset="UTF-8"/><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width"/><meta name="description" content="A reader’s 1959 Favorit F11, preserved with its receipt, club membership card and photographs of its first owner in Serbia."/><link rel="canonical" href="https://teob.dk/en/bikes/favorit-f11-1959/"/><link rel="alternate" hreflang="da" href="https://teob.dk/cykler/favorit-f11-1959/"/><link rel="alternate" hreflang="en" href="https://teob.dk/en/bikes/favorit-f11-1959/"/><link rel="alternate" hreflang="x-default" href="https://teob.dk/cykler/favorit-f11-1959/"/><meta property="og:type" content="article"/><meta property="og:title" content="1959 Favorit F11 · A reader’s bicycle"/><meta property="og:description" content="A Czechoslovak Favorit racer with a documented Serbian ownership history and a careful restoration."/><meta property="og:image" content={hero.src}/><meta name="twitter:card" content="summary_large_image"/><title>1959 Favorit F11 · The Evolution of Bikes</title><link rel="stylesheet" href={`${base}/styles/global.css`}/></head><body><EnglishHeader current="bikes" danishPath="/cykler/favorit-f11-1959/"/>
<main class="atala-page"><header class="quick-hero"><p class="section-label">Reader’s bicycle · Czechoslovakia / Serbia · 1959</p><h1>Favorit<br/><em>F11</em></h1><p>A gold steel racer with frame number 59F18033, bought in Pančevo in 1960 and preserved with the first owner’s club card and photographs.</p></header>
<style is:global>.favorit-bike-hero picture{display:block;width:min(100%,1100px);margin:0 auto}.favorit-bike-hero picture img{display:block;width:100%!important;height:auto!important;aspect-ratio:auto!important;object-fit:contain!important;filter:none!important}.atala-opening>p.favorit-reader-note{max-width:760px;font-size:clamp(24px,2.2vw,34px)!important;line-height:1.35!important}</style>
<figure class="quick-pass favorit-bike-hero"><OptimizedImage src={hero} alt="Restored gold 1959 Favorit F11 seen from the drive side" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high"/><figcaption>The Favorit F11 after Stefan Đurić’s restoration. Photograph: Stefan Đurić.</figcaption></figure>
<section class="atala-facts"><div><strong>1959</strong><span>Frame-number year</span></div><div><strong>F11</strong><span>Model assessment</span></div><div><strong>1960</strong><span>Bought in Pančevo</span></div><div><strong>59F18033</strong><span>Frame number</span></div></section>
<section class="atala-opening"><p class="section-label">Not part of the collection</p><p class="favorit-reader-note">This bicycle belongs to reader Stefan Đurić and is presented as a reader contribution. It is not part of The Evolution of Bikes collection. See more from his workshop on the <a href="https://www.facebook.com/profile.php?id=100095668024101" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Numenor Cycles Facebook page</a> and under <strong>#NumenorCycles</strong>.</p></section>
<section class="atala-story"><div><p class="section-label">Provenance</p><h2>From Srbinko to Stefan</h2></div><div><p>The first owner, Srbinko Drakšan, bought the bicycle on 1 December 1960 and rode with the Avala club in Belgrade. His family preserved the receipt, membership card and photographs from his youth.</p><p>Stefan Đurić later bought the bicycle from the family and restored it at his Numenor Cycles workshop. The original gold finish was retained, while the deteriorated transfers were replaced with reproductions.</p><p><a href={`${base}/en/stories/favorit-f11-en-cykel-og-en-ungdom/`}>Read the full story of the bicycle and its first owner.</a></p></div></section>
<section class="atala-details"><figure><OptimizedImage src={crank} alt="Favorit chainset and front derailleur on the restored F11"/><figcaption>Favorit chainset and front derailleur.</figcaption></figure><figure><OptimizedImage src={derailleur} alt="Favorit rear derailleur, freewheel and chain"/><figcaption>The Favorit rear derailleur and five-speed freewheel.</figcaption></figure><figure><OptimizedImage src={stem} alt="Favorit stem marked Made in Czechoslovakia"/><figcaption>The stem is marked “Favorit – Made in Czechoslovakia”.</figcaption></figure></section>
<section class="koga-specs"><div><p class="section-label">Brief specification</p><h2>What is documented</h2></div><dl><div><dt>Make and model</dt><dd>Favorit F11, identified by Milan Moravec</dd></div><div><dt>Year</dt><dd>1959 according to the interpretation of the frame number</dd></div><div><dt>Purchased</dt><dd>1 December 1960 in Pančevo</dd></div><div><dt>First owner</dt><dd>Srbinko Drakšan</dd></div><div><dt>Frame</dt><dd>Lugged steel, original gold finish</dd></div><div><dt>Equipment</dt><dd>Predominantly Favorit; original according to the restorer</dd></div><div><dt>Restoration</dt><dd>Stefan Đurić, Numenor Cycles</dd></div><div><dt>Status</dt><dd>Reader’s bicycle · not in the collection</dd></div></dl></section>
<section class="reader-bike-gallery"><header><p class="section-label">Image gallery</p><h2>From discovery to completed bicycle</h2><p>Details of the bicycle, its restoration and the papers that accompanied it.</p></header><div class="reader-bike-gallery-grid">{gallery.map(([image, caption, alt]) => <figure><OptimizedImage src={image} alt={alt}/><figcaption>{caption}</figcaption></figure>)}</div></section>
<section class="atala-closing"><p>The receipt and club card make this F11 more than an attractive old racing bicycle. They tell us whose hands first rested on its bars.</p><div class="bike-bottom-nav"><a href={`${base}/en/bikes/`}>← Back to the bicycles</a><a href={`${base}/en/stories/favorit-f11-en-cykel-og-en-ungdom/`}>Read the story →</a></div></section></main><EnglishFooter/></body></html>
<style>.reader-bike-gallery{max-width:1180px;margin:1rem auto 6rem;padding:0 1.5rem}.reader-bike-gallery>header{max-width:720px;margin-bottom:2rem}.reader-bike-gallery h2{font:400 clamp(2.2rem,5vw,4rem)/1.05 'Libre Caslon Display',serif;margin:.55rem 0 1rem}.reader-bike-gallery>header>p:last-child{font-size:1.05rem;line-height:1.65}.reader-bike-gallery-grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,minmax(0,1fr));gap:2rem 1.25rem}.reader-bike-gallery figure{margin:0}.reader-bike-gallery picture{display:block;height:300px;overflow:hidden;background:#e9e4d8}.reader-bike-gallery :global(img){width:100%;height:100%;object-fit:cover}.reader-bike-gallery figcaption{margin-top:.7rem;color:#625e55;font-size:.84rem;line-height:1.5}@media(max-width:800px){.reader-bike-gallery-grid{grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr}.reader-bike-gallery picture{height:240px}}@media(max-width:520px){.reader-bike-gallery-grid{grid-template-columns:1fr}.reader-bike-gallery picture{height:auto}.reader-bike-gallery :global(img){height:auto}}</style>
